Task 1: Environment Setup and Jenkins Installation
Subtask 1.1: Update System and Install Prerequisites
First, update your system and install necessary dependencies:

# Update package lists
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install required packages
sudo apt install -y wget curl gnupg2 software-properties-common apt-transport-https ca-certificates
Subtask 1.2: Install Java (OpenJDK 11)
Jenkins requires Java to run. Install OpenJDK 11:

# Install OpenJDK 11
sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk

# Verify Java installation
java -version
javac -version

# Set JAVA_HOME environment variable
echo 'export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
echo $JAVA_HOME
Subtask 1.3: Install Jenkins
Install Jenkins using the official repository:

# Add Jenkins repository key
curl -fsSL https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc > /dev/null

# Add Jenkins repository
echo deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null

# Update package lists and install Jenkins
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y jenkins

# Start and enable Jenkins service
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins

# Check Jenkins status
sudo systemctl status jenkins
Subtask 1.4: Initial Jenkins Setup
Access Jenkins and complete the initial setup:

# Get the initial admin password
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
Open a web browser and navigate to http://localhost:8080
Enter the initial admin password from the command above
Select Install suggested plugins
Create an admin user with the following details:
Username: admin
Password: admin123
Full name: Jenkins Administrator
Email: admin@localhost
Keep the default Jenkins URL: http://localhost:8080/
Click Start using Jenkins
Task 2: Install and Configure Docker Plugin
Subtask 2.1: Install Docker Engine
Install Docker on your Linux machine:

# Remove any old Docker installations
sudo apt remove -y docker docker-engine docker.io containerd runc

# Add Docker's official GPG key
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg

# Add Docker repository
echo "deb [arch=amd64 signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu $(lsb_release -cs) stable" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null

# Update package lists and install Docker
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin

# Add jenkins user to docker group
sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

# Start and enable Docker service
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

# Restart Jenkins to apply group changes
sudo systemctl restart jenkins

# Verify Docker installation
sudo docker --version
sudo docker run hello-world
Subtask 2.2: Install Docker Plugin in Jenkins
Navigate to Jenkins dashboard at http://localhost:8080
Click Manage Jenkins → Manage Plugins
Click the Available tab
Search for Docker in the filter box
Select the following plugins:
Docker Pipeline
Docker
Docker Commons Plugin
Click Install without restart
Check Restart Jenkins when installation is complete and no jobs are running
Wait for Jenkins to restart and log back in.

Subtask 2.3: Configure Docker in Jenkins
Configure Docker settings in Jenkins:

Go to Manage Jenkins → Configure System
Scroll down to Docker section
Click Add Docker → Docker
Configure the following:
Name: local-docker
Docker Host URI: unix:///var/run/docker.sock
Check Enabled
Click Test Connection to verify
Click Save
Subtask 2.4: Create a Docker-based Pipeline
Create a new pipeline job to test Docker integration:

Click New Item from Jenkins dashboard
Enter name: docker-pipeline-test
Select Pipeline and click OK
In the Pipeline section, select Pipeline script
Enter the following pipeline code:
pipeline {
    agent any
    
    stages {
        stage('Docker Info') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh 'docker --version'
                    sh 'docker info'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Pull and Run Container') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh 'docker pull alpine:latest'
                    sh 'docker run --rm alpine:latest echo "Hello from Docker container!"'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Build Custom Image') {
            steps {
                script {
                    writeFile file: 'Dockerfile', text: '''
FROM alpine:latest
RUN echo "Custom Docker image built by Jenkins" > /tmp/jenkins-built.txt
CMD cat /tmp/jenkins-built.txt
'''
                    sh 'docker build -t jenkins-test-image .'
                    sh 'docker run --rm jenkins-test-image'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Cleanup') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh 'docker rmi jenkins-test-image || true'
                    sh 'docker system prune -f'
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    post {
        always {
            cleanWs()
        }
    }
}
Click Save
Click Build Now to execute the pipeline
Monitor the build progress in Console Output
Task 3: Install and Configure Maven Plugin
Subtask 3.1: Install Maven on the System
Install Apache Maven:

# Download Maven 3.9.4
cd /opt
sudo wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/maven/maven-3/3.9.4/binaries/apache-maven-3.9.4-bin.tar.gz

# Extract Maven
sudo tar xzf apache-maven-3.9.4-bin.tar.gz
sudo ln -s apache-maven-3.9.4 maven

# Set Maven environment variables
echo 'export M2_HOME=/opt/maven' | sudo tee -a /etc/environment
echo 'export MAVEN_HOME=/opt/maven' | sudo tee -a /etc/environment
echo 'export PATH=${M2_HOME}/bin:${PATH}' | sudo tee -a /etc/environment

# Apply environment changes
source /etc/environment

# Create symbolic link for system-wide access
sudo ln -s /opt/maven/bin/mvn /usr/local/bin/mvn

# Verify Maven installation
mvn -version
Subtask 3.2: Install Maven Plugin in Jenkins
Go to Manage Jenkins → Manage Plugins
Click the Available tab
Search for Maven Integration
Select the following plugins:
Maven Integration plugin
Pipeline Maven Integration Plugin
Click Install without restart
Check Restart Jenkins when installation is complete and no jobs are running
Subtask 3.3: Configure Maven in Jenkins Global Tools
After Jenkins restarts, go to Manage Jenkins → Global Tool Configuration
Scroll to Maven section
Click Add Maven
Configure the following:
Name: Maven-3.9.4
Uncheck Install automatically
MAVEN_HOME: /opt/maven
Scroll to JDK section (if not already configured)
Click Add JDK
Configure the following:
Name: OpenJDK-11
Uncheck Install automatically
JAVA_HOME: /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64
Click Save
Subtask 3.4: Create a Sample Java Project
Create a sample Maven project for testing:

# Create project directory
mkdir -p /tmp/sample-java-project
cd /tmp/sample-java-project

# Create Maven project structure
mkdir -p src/main/java/com/example
mkdir -p src/test/java/com/example

# Create pom.xml
cat > pom.xml << 'EOF'
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 
         http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    
    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>sample-java-app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    
    <name>Sample Java Application</name>
    <description>A simple Java application for Jenkins testing</description>
    
    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.source>11</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>11</maven.compiler.target>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <junit.version>4.13.2</junit.version>
    </properties>
    
    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>junit</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit</artifactId>
            <version>${junit.version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
    
    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.11.0</version>
                <configuration>
                    <source>11</source>
                    <target>11</target>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.1.2</version>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
EOF

# Create main Java class
cat > src/main/java/com/example/HelloWorld.java << 'EOF'
package com.example;

public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World from Jenkins Maven build!");
    }
    
    public String getMessage() {
        return "Hello, World!";
    }
    
    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}
EOF

# Create test class
cat > src/test/java/com/example/HelloWorldTest.java << 'EOF'
package com.example;

import org.junit.Test;
import static org.junit.Assert.*;

public class HelloWorldTest {
    
    @Test
    public void testGetMessage() {
        HelloWorld hw = new HelloWorld();
        assertEquals("Hello, World!", hw.getMessage());
    }
    
    @Test
    public void testAdd() {
        HelloWorld hw = new HelloWorld();
        assertEquals(5, hw.add(2, 3));
        assertEquals(0, hw.add(-1, 1));
    }
}
EOF

# Test Maven build locally
mvn clean compile test package

# Copy project to Jenkins workspace
sudo cp -r /tmp/sample-java-project /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/
sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/sample-java-project
Subtask 3.5: Create Maven Pipeline Job
Create a Jenkins pipeline for the Maven project:

Go to Jenkins dashboard
Click New Item
Enter name: maven-java-pipeline
Select Pipeline and click OK
In the Pipeline section, select Pipeline script
Enter the following pipeline code:
pipeline {
    agent any
    
    tools {
        maven 'Maven-3.9.4'
        jdk 'OpenJDK-11'
    }
    
    environment {
        MAVEN_OPTS = '-Xmx1024m'
    }
    
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // Copy the sample project to workspace
                    sh 'cp -r /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/sample-java-project/* .'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Environment Info') {
            steps {
                sh 'java -version'
                sh 'mvn -version'
                sh 'echo "JAVA_HOME: $JAVA_HOME"'
                sh 'echo "MAVEN_HOME: $MAVEN_HOME"'
            }
        }
        
        stage('Clean') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean'
            }
        }
        
        stage('Compile') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn compile'
            }
        }
        
        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn test'
            }
            post {
                always {
                    publishTestResults testResultsPattern: 'target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Package') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn package -DskipTests'
            }
        }
        
        stage('Archive Artifacts') {
            steps {
                archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'target/*.jar', fingerprint: true
            }
        }
        
        stage('Run Application') {
            steps {
                sh 'java -cp target/sample-java-app-1.0.0.jar com.example.HelloWorld'
            }
        }
    }
    
    post {
        always {
            cleanWs()
        }
        success {
            echo 'Maven build completed successfully!'
        }
        failure {
            echo 'Maven build failed!'
        }
    }
}
Click Save
Click Build Now to execute the pipeline
Monitor the build progress and check each stage
Task 4: Advanced Integration - Docker with Maven
Subtask 4.1: Create Dockerized Maven Build Pipeline
Create an advanced pipeline that combines Docker and Maven:

Create a new pipeline job: dockerized-maven-build
Use the following pipeline script:
pipeline {
    agent any
    
    environment {
        DOCKER_IMAGE = 'maven-app'
        DOCKER_TAG = "${BUILD_NUMBER}"
    }
    
    stages {
        stage('Prepare Workspace') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // Copy sample project
                    sh 'cp -r /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/sample-java-project/* .'
                    
                    // Create Dockerfile for the application
                    writeFile file: 'Dockerfile', text: '''
FROM openjdk:11-jre-slim

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/sample-java-app-1.0.0.jar app.jar

EXPOSE 8080

CMD ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
'''
                    
                    // Create multi-stage Dockerfile for build
                    writeFile file: 'Dockerfile.build', text: '''
FROM maven:3.9.4-openjdk-11 AS build

WORKDIR /app

COPY pom.xml .
RUN mvn dependency:go-offline -B

COPY src ./src
RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests

FROM openjdk:11-jre-slim

WORKDIR /app

COPY --from=build /app/target/sample-java-app-1.0.0.jar app.jar

CMD ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
'''
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Build with Maven in Docker') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // Build using Maven Docker container
                    sh '''
                        docker run --rm \
                        -v "$(pwd)":/usr/src/app \
                        -w /usr/src/app \
                        maven:3.9.4-openjdk-11 \
                        mvn clean package -DskipTests
                    '''
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Test with Maven in Docker') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh '''
                        docker run --rm \
                        -v "$(pwd)":/usr/src/app \
                        -w /usr/src/app \
                        maven:3.9.4-openjdk-11 \
                        mvn test
                    '''
                }
            }
            post {
                always {
                    publishTestResults testResultsPattern: 'target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Build Docker Image') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh "docker build -t ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${DOCKER_TAG} ."
                    sh "docker build -t ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:latest ."
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Test Docker Image') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh "docker run --rm ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${DOCKER_TAG}"
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Multi-stage Docker Build') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh "docker build -f Dockerfile.build -t ${DOCKER_IMAGE}-multistage:${DOCKER_TAG} ."
                    sh "docker run --rm ${DOCKER_IMAGE}-multistage:${DOCKER_TAG}"
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Image Information') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh "docker images | grep ${DOCKER_IMAGE}"
                    sh "docker inspect ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${DOCKER_TAG}"
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    post {
        always {
            script {
                // Cleanup Docker images
                sh "docker rmi ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${DOCKER_TAG} || true"
                sh "docker rmi ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:latest || true"
                sh "docker rmi ${DOCKER_IMAGE}-multistage:${DOCKER_TAG} || true"
                sh "docker system prune -f"
            }
            cleanWs()
        }
    }
}
Save and run the pipeline
